From 1297989658e006cb32367cace1c72dc8003f2230 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Be <m.gonser@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:10:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat: files explorer as a real, toggleable sidebar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The explorer panel used to float above the canvas as an absolutely
positioned overlay that started below the toolbar row and had to fight
Excalidraw's z-index stack. It is now a proper layout column:

- excalidraw-app renders a flex row (sidebar | canvas), so the canvas
  never sits under the panel; Excalidraw resizes via its ResizeObserver.
- The panel keeps living inside <Excalidraw> (its dialogs need the
  editor context) but is portaled into the sidebar column; the portal
  root carries `excalidraw` + theme class so CSS variables resolve, and
  paints an opaque background so nothing shows through.
- Visible by default, collapsible via the header button, the floating
  "Files" island button, the new main menu entry or Alt+F. Open state
  and width are persisted in localStorage.
- Width is drag-resizable (200–520px, keyboard-adjustable separator).
- Below 730px the sidebar overlays the canvas with a backdrop instead of
  squeezing it, and starts collapsed.
- Tree glyphs (☰ ▰ ◇ ⋮ ▾) replaced by inline SVG icons in
  ExplorerIcons.tsx, used by the panel and the open dialog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
